# Shell scripts run on Linux hosts and CI runners, including the copies inside
# release bundles built on Windows. A CRLF checkout gives the shebang a trailing
# carriage return and breaks execution there, so pin them to LF everywhere
# (core.autocrlf=true otherwise rewrites them on a Windows clone).
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for the Python helpers in scripts/: they carry a shebang and
# run on Linux runners, where a CRLF checkout would produce spurious diffs and
# CRLF-terminated report output.
*.py text eol=lf
